                <pb facs="0118" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg46"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5072/42.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Turkish Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Ottoman Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May 19,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    advise your excellency that His Excellency Rifaat Pasha, minister of foreign
                    affairs, exchanged to-day with the Bulgarian delegate the protocol by which we
                    recognize the new political State of Bulgaria.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Kiazim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
